## ads_get_lint_rules
Returns documentation for **Constellation** (Atlassian Design System) ESLint rules shipped with this MCP—rule purpose, examples, and fixes where available.

WHAT YOU GET:
- No `terms`: JSON array of all rule payloads.
- With `terms`: fuzzy search (or exact rule name when `exactName` is true); JSON for one or more matching rules.

WHEN TO USE:
Explaining or fixing an ESLint message from ADS rules (e.g. `icon-label`, `ensure-proper-xcss-usage`, `no-deprecated-apis`), or browsing rule docs without opening the repo. Prefer this over guessing from rule id alone.

This tool does not run ESLint; it only returns bundled documentation.
args: {"terms":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"default":[],"description":"Search terms matched against rule name, description, and docs body (fuzzy unless `exactName` is true). Example: `[\"icon-label\", \"xcss\", \"design token\"]`. Omit or empty: return **all** rules as JSON."},"limit":{"type":"number","default":1,"description":"Max matches **per term** when searching (default 1). Not used when returning all rules."},"exactName":{"type":"boolean","default":false,"description":"If true, resolve each term by **exact** ESLint rule name (case-insensitive). If false, fuzzy search across name, description, and content."}}

## atlaskit_get_components
Returns a compact inventory of public `@atlaskit/*` and internal `@atlassian/*` Platform component packages that are not covered by the Atlassian Design System (ADS) component catalog. Output is names and packages only.

WHEN TO USE:
Use this for fallback discovery after ADS component search is not enough, or when you need to see which non-ADS components are available without the full metadata payload. For implementation examples and props, use `atlaskit_search_components`.

Internal Atlassian packages are not available for use outside Atlassian.

No parameters.
args: {}

## atlaskit_search_components
Searches the bundled non-ADS component catalog, including public `@atlaskit/*` packages and internal `@atlassian/*` Platform offerings, outside the Atlassian Design System (ADS) component catalog. Returns JSON objects with **name**, **package**, **description**, **examples**, and **props** for each match (trimmed payload).

WHEN TO USE:
Use this for fallback research when `ads_search_components` or `ads_plan.components` does not find a useful ADS component, or when the user asks about a specific non-ADS `@atlaskit/*` or `@atlassian/*` package. Prefer canonical ADS components first for standard UI. Internal Atlassian packages are not available for use outside Atlassian.
